{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773084256,"nonce":"/CY3hgKBle7nsGMGS0ZF7b6gus4=","title":"Issue cross-references: #id syntax and navigable hyperlinks","message":"Agents referencing related issues in commit messages, comments, and issue descriptions currently do so in free text with no structural linkage. We should:\n\n1. Adopt a canonical syntax for issue cross-references — `#\u003cshort-id\u003e` (first 7 chars of git-bug ID, matching the human_id format) — so references are parseable and consistent\n2. Parse these references in issue descriptions and comments when rendering in the dashboard, converting them to navigable `#/issues?repo=\u003crepo\u003e\u0026issue=\u003cid\u003e` hash links (similar to GitHub issue references)\n3. Document this as a policy in CLAUDE.md: when an agent is implementing something directly related to another issue it has in context, it should reference it with `#short-id` in the issue description, comments, and commit message body\n\nThis is a prerequisite for meaningful issue-to-issue navigation in the planned GraphView (umbrella→child edges, related-work edges) and for making the issue graph structurally complete rather than relying on label inference.","files":null}]}